meta {
  name: Person not found
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/persons/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 404
}

docs {
  A row you cannot reach answers 404, never 403. The two cases - the row does
  not exist, and the row exists but is outside your scope - are deliberately
  indistinguishable, because a 403 would confirm the row is there. Expect 404
  from every id-addressed route on this surface for both.

  403 on this surface means something else: the capability itself was refused
  before any row was looked at.
}
